<!--
    FORK: Slovak texts, used when the watch language is Slovak (see monkey.jungle). Every other
    watch language gets Czech. Covers every id of resources-ces and resources-fork, in the same
    order; an id missing here would show the Czech text on a Slovak watch.

    Sources:
    - Verím v Boha: Jednotný katolícky spevník, 2nd ed., SSV Trnava 2006, p. 9 (as quoted by
      sk.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apoštolské_vyznanie_viery).
    - Zdravas', Kráľovná: Liturgia hodín, Mariánske antifóny
      (breviar.upc.uniba.sk/ordinar/ord_km.htm). The closing versicle "Oroduj za nás, svätá Božia
      Rodička..." as in sk.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruženec_(modlitba).
    - Mysteries inserted into the Hail Mary and the introductory petitions per set:
      sk.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruženec_(modlitba) (cites dmc.sk); the same wording is on
      opusdei.org/sk-sk/article/svaty-ruzenec. Luminous mysteries: the main screen shows the
      shorter version approved by KBS in March 2003 (tkkbs.sk), the meditation view the full one.
    - Ó, Ježišu (Fatima prayer): sk.wikibooks.org/wiki/Modlitby/Ruženec.
    - Modlime sa: collect of the feast of Our Lady of the Rosary, dominikani.sk
      (Ružencovej Panny Márie), with the short conclusion "Skrze Krista, nášho Pána."
    - Bible quotations and book abbreviations in the meditations: Sväté písmo, SSV 1996
      (svatepismo.sk).
    Translated from the Czech/English upstream texts, to be proofread by a Slovak speaker:
    meditations, help, menus, hints, fruits of the mysteries, abbreviated titles.

    One line = one phrase in the prayer texts; the text view keeps these line breaks.
-->
